{"title":"The diagonal argument, made visible","sub":"If a perfect halting-predictor H existed, this table of its predictions would have to include a program that breaks it.","kind":"grid","interval":1500,"grid":{"rowLabels":["M1","M2","M3","M4","M5","D"],"colLabels":["⟨M1⟩","⟨M2⟩","⟨M3⟩","⟨M4⟩","⟨M5⟩","⟨D⟩"]},"legend":[["b","diagonal entry being read"],["c","diagonal"],["a","D does the opposite"],["bad","contradiction"]],"frames":[{"caption":"Suppose a program <b>H</b> could predict, for any program and any input, whether it halts. Fill in a table with its predictions: row = a program, column = the code it is given as input.","cells":[["halt","loop","halt","halt","loop","…"],["loop","loop","halt","loop","halt","…"],["halt","halt","halt","loop","loop","…"],["loop","halt","loop","loop","halt","…"],["halt","loop","loop","halt","halt","…"],["","","","","",""]],"cellCls":{}},{"caption":"Every program that could ever be written appears somewhere in this list of rows, since programs are just finite strings.","cells":[["halt","loop","halt","halt","loop","…"],["loop","loop","halt","loop","halt","…"],["halt","halt","halt","loop","loop","…"],["loop","halt","loop","loop","halt","…"],["halt","loop","loop","halt","halt","…"],["","","","","",""]],"cellCls":{"0,0":"muted","0,1":"muted","0,2":"muted","0,3":"muted","0,4":"muted","1,0":"muted","1,1":"muted","1,2":"muted","1,3":"muted","1,4":"muted","2,0":"muted","2,1":"muted","2,2":"muted","2,3":"muted","2,4":"muted","3,0":"muted","3,1":"muted","3,2":"muted","3,3":"muted","3,4":"muted","4,0":"muted","4,1":"muted","4,2":"muted","4,3":"muted","4,4":"muted"}},{"caption":"The diagonal: what does <b>M1</b> do when fed its <i>own</i> code? H says <b>halt</b>.","cells":[["halt","loop","halt","halt","loop","…"],["loop","loop","halt","loop","halt","…"],["halt","halt","halt","loop","loop","…"],["loop","halt","loop","loop","halt","…"],["halt","loop","loop","halt","halt","…"],["","","","","",""]],"cellCls":{"0,0":"b"}},{"caption":"Build a new program <b>D</b> that does the <b>opposite</b>: on input ⟨M1⟩, D will loop.","cells":[["halt","loop","halt","halt","loop","…"],["loop","loop","halt","loop","halt","…"],["halt","halt","halt","loop","loop","…"],["loop","halt","loop","loop","halt","…"],["halt","loop","loop","halt","halt","…"],["loop","","","","",""]],"cellCls":{"0,0":"c","5,0":"a"}},{"caption":"The diagonal: what does <b>M2</b> do when fed its <i>own</i> code? H says <b>loop</b>.","cells":[["halt","loop","halt","halt","loop","…"],["loop","loop","halt","loop","halt","…"],["halt","halt","halt","loop","loop","…"],["loop","halt","loop","loop","halt","…"],["halt","loop","loop","halt","halt","…"],["loop","","","","",""]],"cellCls":{"0,0":"c","1,1":"b","5,0":"a"}},{"caption":"Build a new program <b>D</b> that does the <b>opposite</b>: on input ⟨M2⟩, D will halt.","cells":[["halt","loop","halt","halt","loop","…"],["loop","loop","halt","loop","halt","…"],["halt","halt","halt","loop","loop","…"],["loop","halt","loop","loop","halt","…"],["halt","loop","loop","halt","halt","…"],["loop","halt","","","",""]],"cellCls":{"0,0":"c","1,1":"c","5,0":"a","5,1":"a"}},{"caption":"The diagonal: what does <b>M3</b> do when fed its <i>own</i> code? H says <b>halt</b>.","cells":[["halt","loop","halt","halt","loop","…"],["loop","loop","halt","loop","halt","…"],["halt","halt","halt","loop","loop","…"],["loop","halt","loop","loop","halt","…"],["halt","loop","loop","halt","halt","…"],["loop","halt","","","",""]],"cellCls":{"0,0":"c","1,1":"c","2,2":"b","5,0":"a","5,1":"a"}},{"caption":"Build a new program <b>D</b> that does the <b>opposite</b>: on input ⟨M3⟩, D will loop.","cells":[["halt","loop","halt","halt","loop","…"],["loop","loop","halt","loop","halt","…"],["halt","halt","halt","loop","loop","…"],["loop","halt","loop","loop","halt","…"],["halt","loop","loop","halt","halt","…"],["loop","halt","loop","","",""]],"cellCls":{"0,0":"c","1,1":"c","2,2":"c","5,0":"a","5,1":"a","5,2":"a"}},{"caption":"The diagonal: what does <b>M4</b> do when fed its <i>own</i> code? H says <b>loop</b>.","cells":[["halt","loop","halt","halt","loop","…"],["loop","loop","halt","loop","halt","…"],["halt","halt","halt","loop","loop","…"],["loop","halt","loop","loop","halt","…"],["halt","loop","loop","halt","halt","…"],["loop","halt","loop","","",""]],"cellCls":{"0,0":"c","1,1":"c","2,2":"c","3,3":"b","5,0":"a","5,1":"a","5,2":"a"}},{"caption":"Build a new program <b>D</b> that does the <b>opposite</b>: on input ⟨M4⟩, D will halt.","cells":[["halt","loop","halt","halt","loop","…"],["loop","loop","halt","loop","halt","…"],["halt","halt","halt","loop","loop","…"],["loop","halt","loop","loop","halt","…"],["halt","loop","loop","halt","halt","…"],["loop","halt","loop","halt","",""]],"cellCls":{"0,0":"c","1,1":"c","2,2":"c","3,3":"c","5,0":"a","5,1":"a","5,2":"a","5,3":"a"}},{"caption":"The diagonal: what does <b>M5</b> do when fed its <i>own</i> code? H says <b>halt</b>.","cells":[["halt","loop","halt","halt","loop","…"],["loop","loop","halt","loop","halt","…"],["halt","halt","halt","loop","loop","…"],["loop","halt","loop","loop","halt","…"],["halt","loop","loop","halt","halt","…"],["loop","halt","loop","halt","",""]],"cellCls":{"0,0":"c","1,1":"c","2,2":"c","3,3":"c","4,4":"b","5,0":"a","5,1":"a","5,2":"a","5,3":"a"}},{"caption":"Build a new program <b>D</b> that does the <b>opposite</b>: on input ⟨M5⟩, D will loop.","cells":[["halt","loop","halt","halt","loop","…"],["loop","loop","halt","loop","halt","…"],["halt","halt","halt","loop","loop","…"],["loop","halt","loop","loop","halt","…"],["halt","loop","loop","halt","halt","…"],["loop","halt","loop","halt","loop",""]],"cellCls":{"0,0":"c","1,1":"c","2,2":"c","3,3":"c","4,4":"c","5,0":"a","5,1":"a","5,2":"a","5,3":"a","5,4":"a"}},{"caption":"D is a perfectly ordinary program: ask H, then do the opposite. So D must be one of the rows. But which one? It differs from every row exactly where that row meets the diagonal.","cells":[["halt","loop","halt","halt","loop","…"],["loop","loop","halt","loop","halt","…"],["halt","halt","halt","loop","loop","…"],["loop","halt","loop","loop","halt","…"],["halt","loop","loop","halt","halt","…"],["loop","halt","loop","halt","loop",""]],"cellCls":{"0,0":"c","1,1":"c","2,2":"c","3,3":"c","4,4":"c","5,0":"a","5,1":"a","5,2":"a","5,3":"a","5,4":"a"}},{"caption":"And on its own code, ⟨D⟩? If H says D halts, D loops. If H says D loops, D halts. <b>No answer is possible</b>, so H cannot exist. No program decides halting.","cells":[["halt","loop","halt","halt","loop","…"],["loop","loop","halt","loop","halt","…"],["halt","halt","halt","loop","loop","…"],["loop","halt","loop","loop","halt","…"],["halt","loop","loop","halt","halt","…"],["loop","halt","loop","halt","loop","?!"]],"cellCls":{"0,0":"c","1,1":"c","2,2":"c","3,3":"c","4,4":"c","5,0":"a","5,1":"a","5,2":"a","5,3":"a","5,4":"a","5,5":"bad"}}]}